<header class="wrap top"><a class="brand" href="#top"><span class="brandseal" aria-hidden="true">GCG</span><span class="brandname">Gourmet Crunch &amp; Glaze<small>Founded by Chef Tom · Rustic heritage, culinary science</small></span></a><nav><a href="#soups">Soups</a><a href="#chicken">Chicken</a><a href="#story">Our story</a><a class="cta" href="#feedback">Share your view ↗</a></nav></header>
<main id="top"><section class="wrap hero"><div><div class="eyebrow">A new kind of comfort</div><h1>Rustic roots.<br><em>Engineered flavour.</em></h1><p>A first look at Gourmet Crunch &amp; Glaze, founded by Chef Tom. We bring a chef’s eye to the meeting point of rustic heritage and culinary science, shaping ideas for food with character, craft and contrast.</p><div class="note">A premium food concept · London</div><a class="button" href="#soups">Explore the first three &nbsp; ↓</a></div><div class="visual"><img src="https://www.agrodolce.it/app/uploads/2024/11/zuppa-di-patate-e-porri.jpg" alt="Creamy potato and leek soup with golden croutons"><div class="stamp"><b>GCG · CHEF TOM</b>Rustic roots<br>culinary science</div><div class="caption">Illustrative serving image</div></div></section><div class="strip"><span>Classic recipes</span><i>•</i><span>Modern chef's touch</span><i>•</i><span>Made for a proper lunch</span></div>
<section class="wrap menu" id="soups"><div class="heading"><div class="eyebrow">A first taste</div><h2>Three soups.<br>Which one calls to you?</h2><p>Inspired by the Gourmet Crunch &amp; Glaze soup concepts. These earlier roadmap prices are here to test interest and are under review. Each soup lunch-box concept is shown with a separate tub of signature fresh, seasoned croutons. No food is currently for sale.</p></div><div class="cards">
<article class="card"><div class="photo pair"><img class="dish" loading="lazy" src="soup-ayrshire-leek.jpg" alt="Ayrshire potato and garden leek soup with crisp croutons"><div class="origin"><img loading="lazy" src="potato-field.jpg" alt="Ayrshire potato fields from the supplied concept imagery"></div><span class="tag">Garden favourite</span></div><div class="body"><div class="kicker">01 · Vegetarian idea</div><h3>Ayrshire Potato<br>&amp; Garden Leek</h3><p>A cold-weather pairing of earthy Ayrshire potatoes and sweet garden leeks. Inspired by Scotland’s west-coast harvests, with a naturally silky body and fresh garden notes.</p><div class="foot"><div class="price">£35.50<small>single lunch box · 500 ml pot</small><span class="share">£62.00<small>2-person sharing box</small></span></div><span class="crouton">separate crouton tub</span></div></div></article>
<article class="card"><div class="photo pair"><img class="dish" loading="lazy" src="soup-french-onion.jpg" alt="French onion soup crowned with toasted cheese croutons"><div class="origin"><img loading="lazy" src="onion-field.jpg" alt="Onion crop rows"><img loading="lazy" src="onion-harvest.jpg" alt="Freshly harvested onions"></div><span class="tag">The French classic</span></div><div class="body"><div class="kicker">02 · Slow-cooked comfort</div><h3>Classical French<br>Onion</h3><p>An old French classic with deeply caramelised onions, savoury broth and fragrant herbs. The Versailles legend gives this comforting bowl a touch of royal drama.</p><div class="foot"><div class="price">£35.50<small>single lunch box · 500 ml pot</small><span class="share">£62.00<small>2-person sharing box</small></span></div><span class="crouton">separate crouton tub</span></div></div></article>
<article class="card"><div class="photo pair"><img class="dish" loading="lazy" src="soup-creme-de-barry.jpg" alt="Crème de Barry cauliflower soup with croutons and chives"><div class="origin"><img loading="lazy" src="madame-du-barry-portrait.jpg" alt="Portrait associated with the Crème de Barry story"></div><span class="tag">A little regal</span></div><div class="body"><div class="kicker">03 · French-inspired</div><h3>Crème de Barry</h3><p>Inspired by the courtly tale of Madame du Barry and her favourite winter cauliflower. Delicate, nutty and velvety, finished with fresh chives.</p><div class="foot"><div class="price">£35.50<small>single lunch box · 500 ml pot</small><span class="share">£62.00<small>2-person sharing box</small></span></div><span class="crouton">separate crouton tub</span></div></div></article></div></section>
<section class="wrap menu" id="chicken" style="padding-top:0"><div class="heading"><div class="eyebrow">The Chicken Lab</div><h2>And a little more<br>than soup.</h2><p>Chicken meal concepts from the roadmap, shown with proposed research prices.</p></div><div class="cards">
<article class="card"><div class="photo"><img loading="lazy" src="https://hips.hearstapps.com/hmg-prod/images/delish-230502-06-fried-chicken-0887-eb-lead-645ec6f9a226a.jpg?resize=1200:*" alt="Golden, crunchy fried chicken pieces"><span class="tag">The crunch classic</span></div><div class="body"><div class="kicker">04 · Air-fryer chicken kit</div><h3>High-Shatter<br>Chicken Feast</h3><p>The Ultimate Desktop Fry-Up: bone-in legs, thighs and wings with a high-crunch coating, signature savoury glaze and golden potato wedges. The proposed solo box also includes an artisan roll and fruit cupcake.</p><details class="kit-info"><summary>More information</summary><div class="kit-detail"><p><strong>Proposed kit:</strong> in-house-butchered bone-in chicken in a 24-hour buttermilk brine, secret high-shatter dredge pack, signature savoury glaze tub, seasoned potato wedges, one Brakes artisan roll and one premium fruit cupcake. Solo feast-box concept: £49.50 (price under review).</p><h4>The high-shatter shake</h4><ol><li>Pour the dredge into a wide bowl or clean food bag.</li><li>Lift the chicken from the marinade and let excess drip away.</li><li>Press each piece into the dredge until coated. Rest the coated chicken for 2 minutes so the coating can adhere.</li></ol><h4>Draft cooking methods</h4><ul><li><strong>Air fry:</strong> 180°C for 22–25 minutes, turning halfway. Leave space around the pieces.</li><li><strong>Shallow fry:</strong> about 2 cm of neutral high-heat oil at 170°C; fry for 6–8 minutes per side.</li><li><strong>Oven bake:</strong> on a wire rack at 190°C fan / 210°C conventional for 25–30 minutes.</li></ul><p class="cook-note">These are draft concept timings, not final product instructions; cuts and appliances vary. Any chicken must be cooked thoroughly. Check the thickest part with a clean food thermometer: 75°C for 30 seconds, or another safe time-temperature combination. <a href="https://www.food.gov.uk/safety-hygiene/cooking-your-food" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">See Food Standards Agency cooking guidance</a>.</p><h4>Finish and serve</h4><p>Toss the freshly cooked chicken thoroughly in the glaze and serve straight away with the potato wedges.</p></div></details><div class="foot"><div class="price">£49.50<small>proposed · solo feast box</small></div><span class="crouton">legs · thighs · wings</span></div></div></article>
<article class="card"><div class="photo"><img loading="lazy" src="https://scottishscran.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/08/Balmoral-Chicken-Recipe-33-1024x683.jpg" alt="Balmoral chicken wrapped in bacon with haggis stuffing"><span class="tag">A Scottish showpiece</span></div><div class="body"><div class="kicker">05 · Balmoral chicken feast</div><h3>Haggis &amp; Bacon<br>Chicken Balmoral</h3><p>A 250g+ buttermilk-brined chicken breast filled with peppery haggis, wrapped in smoky bacon, with glazed potatoes and whisky sauce.</p><details class="kit-info"><summary>More information</summary><div class="kit-detail"><p><strong>Proposed feast:</strong> 250g+ chicken breast before stuffing, 24-hour buttermilk brine, peppery artisan haggis, smoky back bacon, mustard-herb-mint glazed new potatoes, signature whisky sauce, one Brakes artisan roll and one premium fruit cupcake. Solo box: £54.50. Two-person sharing box: £89.50. Prices under review.</p><h4>1 · Brown the Balmoral chicken</h4><ol><li>Heat a pan over medium-high heat with a little oil. Place the stuffed breast seam-side down and sear for 2–3 minutes. Turn and brown the top for 2 minutes.</li><li>Transfer to a tray and roast at 180°C fan / 200°C conventional for 20–22 minutes, or air fry at 180°C for about 18 minutes. Rest for 5 minutes before slicing.</li></ol><h4>2 · Glaze the potatoes</h4><p>The concept uses par-cooked new potatoes coated in mustard, garden herbs and mint. Place them on the tray for the final 12–15 minutes so the glaze can caramelise.</p><h4>3 · Warm the whisky sauce</h4><p>Warm the sauce gently in a small saucepan or microwave-safe container until steaming hot, about 45–60 seconds in a microwave. Slice the chicken and serve over the potatoes with the sauce.</p><p class="cook-note">These are draft concept timings, not final product instructions; appliance and portion differences can affect cooking. Any chicken must be cooked thoroughly. Check the centre with a clean food thermometer: 75°C for 30 seconds, or another safe time-temperature combination. Clean the probe after use. <a href="https://www.food.gov.uk/safety-hygiene/cooking-your-food" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">See Food Standards Agency cooking guidance</a>.</p></div></details><div class="foot"><div class="price">£54.50<small>solo feast box</small><span class="share">£89.50<small>2-person sharing box</small></span></div><span class="crouton">a proper centrepiece</span></div></div></article>
<article class="card"><div class="photo"><img loading="lazy" src="https://images.pexels.com/photos/5773964/pexels-photo-5773964.jpeg?cs=srgb&amp;dl=pexels-luisbecerrafotografo-5773964.jpg&amp;fm=jpg" alt="Illustrative photograph of crisp glazed chicken"><span class="tag">Boneless &amp; bold</span></div><div class="body"><div class="kicker">06 · Boneless chicken kit</div><h3>Signature Glaze<br>Chicken Fillet</h3><p>A scored, crisp-coated chicken breast with both signature glazes included, plus seasoned potato wedges, an artisan roll and a fruit cupcake.</p><details class="kit-info"><summary>More information</summary><div class="kit-detail"><p><strong>Two glazes in every proposed kit.</strong> No choosing between flavours: the concept includes a tub of each signature glaze, alongside the chicken, seasoned potato wedges, one artisan roll and one premium fruit cupcake. Solo feast-box concept: £44.50 (proposed price under review).</p><h4>Lab batch #1 · Dripping hot honey, mustard &amp; coriander</h4><p>The proposed profile is thick, glossy, sweet-and-sharp, with gentle warmth and herbal notes. Its recipe direction pairs British honey with wholegrain, stone-ground mustard, crushed coriander and a measured touch of aged cayenne. The intended finish is a clingy glaze brushed over the hot scored breast near the end of cooking, or tossed with hot chicken for a lacquered coating.</p><h4>Lab batch #2 · Sweet chilli, roasted garlic &amp; fresh lime</h4><p>The proposed profile is bright, citrus-forward and gently sweet-hot. Its recipe direction uses whole garlic bulbs, slow-roasted for around 90 minutes until soft and mellow, folded into a sweet chilli reduction. Fresh lime juice and finely grated zest are added at the end for a lively citrus finish. Serve it as a dip or drizzle it over the crisp chicken.</p><h4>The chef’s combination</h4><p>For the proposed serving idea, slice the hot chicken into medallions and spoon the hot honey glaze over the meat. Serve the roasted-garlic and lime glaze alongside as a dip for the crunchy coating.</p><p class="cook-note">These are concept flavour directions; recipes, ingredients and sourcing would be developed and confirmed before any product is offered. Food photograph is illustrative and may not show this exact kit or its sides.</p></div></details><div class="foot"><div class="price">£44.50<small>proposed · solo feast box</small></div><span class="crouton">both glazes included</span></div></div></article></div></section>
