<section class="wrap story" id="story"><div class="storygrid"><img loading="lazy" src="https://static.toprecepty.cz/fotky/images/15/14260-1920-1080.jpg" alt="A bowl of soup with herbs and golden croutons"><div><div class="eyebrow">Founded by Chef Tom</div><h2>Rustic heritage.<br>Culinary science.</h2><p>Gourmet Crunch &amp; Glaze is a food concept founded by Chef Tom, drawing on 40 years of professional chef experience. We sit at the intersection of time-honoured cooking and careful culinary exploration: ideas shaped to bring out flavour, texture and character in premium ingredients.</p><p>We do not just make food; we engineer gastronomic experiences. That is the ambition behind the concept—not a claim that products are already made or available.</p><p>This is a market-research showroom. The dishes, methods and prices are ideas to explore; no food is currently for sale.</p><div class="signature">Chef Tom · Founder</div></div></div><div class="roadmap"><div class="eyebrow">Our gastronomic roadmap · concept stages</div><h2>Ideas, explored in phases.</h2><div class="roadmapgrid"><article><div class="kicker">Phase 1 · Soup concepts</div><h3>Gourmet Soup Lab</h3><p>Current market-research focus: rustic, comforting soup ideas exploring long-developed broths and infused vegetable bases. Flavour and texture lead; any future recipes or nutrition claims would need development and validation.</p></article><article><div class="kicker">Phase 2 · Future experiential labs</div><h3>Meal kits · Cakes &amp; bakes · Pizza · Caribbean &amp; Jamaican</h3><p>Future directions could include guided chef-dish kits, pastry ideas shaped by careful hydration and crumb, long-fermented pizza dough with rustic charring, and Caribbean and Jamaican flavours inspired by jerk smoke and rice-box traditions.</p></article><article><div class="kicker">Phase 3 · Freshness-led concepts</div><h3>The Sandwich Formula</h3><p>An idea for well-structured artisan bread pairings, designed around freshness. Any service, timing or delivery model would be considered only in a future business plan.</p></article></div><p class="roadmapnote">These are exploratory concepts, not a launch schedule. Sourcing, methods, products and any future service remain to be developed and validated.</p></div></section></main>
